From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:52:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(kernel-views): pin cgroup group-path validation shapes

### What
Pins `validate_group_path` via `create`: trailing slash, double slash, `..` segment, space/semicolon charset, empty, relative, and over-length paths are each `InvalidPath`; a valid name with dot/dash/underscore is accepted.

### Why it matters
Group paths name virtual cgroup directories; the validator is the traversal/charset gate. The existing tests only exercise one `..` case, so dropping the trailing-slash or charset clause survives the suite.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| drop `ends_with(b"/")` clause | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| drop ASCII charset clause | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-kernel-views --lib group_path_validation`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/cgroup.rs | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/cgroup.rs b/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/cgroup.rs
index 3b4adcfe..8157b7ff 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/cgroup.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/cgroup.rs
@@ -398,4 +398,22 @@ mod tests {
         assert_eq!(cgroups.remove(b"/instance.slice", 0), Err(ViewError::Busy));
         assert_eq!(cgroups.create(b"/../host", 0), Err(ViewError::InvalidPath));
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn group_path_validation_rejects_each_unsafe_shape() {
+        let mut cgroups: CgroupFs<8> = CgroupFs::new();
+        // trailing slash, double slash, dot-dot segment, bad charset, empty, too long
+        assert_eq!(cgroups.create(b"/a/", 0), Err(ViewError::InvalidPath));
+        assert_eq!(cgroups.create(b"/a//b", 0), Err(ViewError::InvalidPath));
+        assert_eq!(cgroups.create(b"/a/../b", 0), Err(ViewError::InvalidPath));
+        assert_eq!(cgroups.create(b"/a b", 0), Err(ViewError::InvalidPath));
+        assert_eq!(cgroups.create(b"/a;b", 0), Err(ViewError::InvalidPath));
+        assert_eq!(cgroups.create(b"", 0), Err(ViewError::InvalidPath));
+        assert_eq!(cgroups.create(b"a", 0), Err(ViewError::InvalidPath));
+        let mut p = [b'a'; 301];
+        p[0] = b'/';
+        assert_eq!(cgroups.create(&p, 0), Err(ViewError::InvalidPath));
+        // valid shapes still accepted (dot and dash and underscore allowed)
+        cgroups.create(b"/ok.slice-1_x", 0).unwrap();
+    }
 }
